<title>JAPAN: Toho Mutual problem loans.</title>
<headline>Toho Mutual problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toho Mutual Life Insurance Co has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	     45.9	     59.4</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  15.7		3.1</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	    4.0		4.0</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    65.6	     66.5</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more.</p>
</text>
